==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ʋɛi̯/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-wei.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɛi̯|s=1}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|wei}}
* {{homophones|nl|wij}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|wei}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*wei}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*hwaij|t=whey}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|f|-|-}}

# a product obtained from [[milk]]; [[whey]] {{defdate|First attested in the early 14th century.}}
#: {{syn|nl|hui|melkwei}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Een van de nevenproducten van melk is '''wei'''.|One of the byproducts of milk is '''whey'''.}}
# {{lb|nl|obsolete}} [[serum]], a component of [[blood]] which does not play a role in [[clotting]]
#: {{syn|nl|serum|bloedserum}}
#: {{uxi|nl|De centrifuge scheidt het stolsel van de '''wei'''.|The centrifuge separates the coagulated blood from the '''serum'''.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|nl|bloedwei}}
* {{l|nl|weiboter}}
* {{l|nl|weikaas}}
* {{l|nl|weiroom}}
* {{l|nl|weivocht}}

===Etymology 2===
Alteration of ''weide'' with regular syncope of intervocalic ''-d-''; compare {{m|nl|weder}} / {{m|nl|weer}}, {{m|nl|leder}} / {{m|nl|leer}}, {{m|nl|lade}} / {{m|nl|la}}, and so forth.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|f|weiden|+}}

# {{alternative form of|nl|weide}}

===Anagrams===
* {{l|nl|wie}}

